System boundary: the unauthenticated GET /live endpoint of the Health API.
Actor: any client. When a client sends GET /live with no request body, the
Health API shall return HTTP 200, Content-Type application/json with no
parameters, and exactly the UTF-8 byte sequence {"status":"live"}. Measure
every request from receipt of complete request headers at the API process
boundary to emission of the final response byte at that boundary. The
maximum is 100 ms, P100, while no more than 25 such requests are in flight;
exactly 25 is included. Non-GET requests, request bodies, error responses,
and higher concurrency are specified separately.
